 "text": "I'm Catalyst, and I check battery material before it's made into cells. This is an anode under a microscope. Grey is graphite. Orange is silicon, which holds far more lithium but swells every charge. Blue is the space the lithium moves through. If the mix is off, lithium can plate out as metal, and in the worst case short the cell and start a fire.",
